WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.070
If you have posttraumatic stress disorder - or PTSD -

2
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.710
it's common to feel like there are places or situations

3
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.980
that are unsafe.

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.450
It may seem like the best option is to avoid them -

5
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.450
staying away from people or places that feel

6
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.120
dangerous, or reminders of a traumatic event.

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.250
As a result, you may develop "I can't" rules:

8
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.260
"I can't leave the house at night.

9
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.590
I can't trust anyone.

10
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.260
I can't handle crowds."

11
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.630
But, these rules won't help you overcome PTSD.

12
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.200
So, how do you learn to say "I can"?

13
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.800
Prolonged Exposure - or PE - is a treatment for PTSD

14
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.540
that helps you do safe things you've been avoiding.

15
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.880
In PE, you and your therapist will practice exposure -

16
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.040
meaning, you'll work to approach things you've steered

17
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.450
clear of since the event.

18
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.620
You have to challenge your "I can't" rules to prove

19
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.790
to yourself that you "can."

20
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.920
Remember when you were learning to swim, or even drive a car?

21
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.530
It was challenging at first, but got easier with practice.

22
00:00:59.530 --> 00:00:61.660
Exposure gets easier with time.

23
00:00:61.660 --> 00:00:64.430
With your therapist, you'll take steps to do the things

24
00:00:64.430 --> 00:00:66.930
that have been hard for you - at your own pace.

25
00:00:66.930 --> 00:00:68.940
So, if you're avoiding the grocery store,

26
00:00:68.940 --> 00:00:71.170
you might start by going when it isn't crowded -

27
00:00:71.170 --> 00:00:73.170
maybe bringing a family member along.

28
00:00:73.170 --> 00:00:75.070
You'll eventually practice going on your own,

29
00:00:75.070 --> 00:00:77.310
perhaps even during peak hours.

30
00:00:77.310 --> 00:00:79.650
With practice, you'll find that you can handle it.

31
00:00:82.280 --> 00:00:84.280
You'll also talk through the details of your

32
00:00:84.280 --> 00:00:86.490
traumatic event in a safe, gradual way with your

33
00:00:86.490 --> 00:00:90.790
therapist. Closing your eyes can help you concentrate.

34
00:00:90.790 --> 00:00:93.190
Retelling the event may sound like the last thing you want to

35
00:00:93.190 --> 00:00:97.460
do - but it helps with emotions like anger, guilt, and sadness.

36
00:00:97.460 --> 00:00:100.900
You'll listen to a recorded version at home, too.

37
00:00:100.900 --> 00:00:103.670
After a few months you'll find that you can talk about your trauma

38
00:00:103.670 --> 00:00:106.010
without feeling so overwhelmed.

39
00:00:106.010 --> 00:00:108.540
Prolonged Exposure doesn't erase your trauma,

40
00:00:108.540 --> 00:00:110.610
but it can help you keep your traumatic experience

41
00:00:110.610 --> 00:00:112.850
from getting in the way of living your life.

42
00:00:112.850 --> 00:00:116.720
PE doesn't require you to take any medications.

43
00:00:116.720 --> 00:00:119.450
With your therapist's help, you'll follow a step-by-step

44
00:00:119.450 --> 00:00:121.550
program for about three months.

45
00:00:121.550 --> 00:00:124.190
Most people who complete PE show noticeable improvement

46
00:00:124.190 --> 00:00:125.330
in their symptoms.

47
00:00:125.330 --> 00:00:127.590
And many no longer have PTSD.

48
00:00:127.590 --> 00:00:130.500
Prolonged Exposure works well for both men and women,

49
00:00:130.500 --> 00:00:133.300
and it's "evidence-based," which means PE has been

50
00:00:133.300 --> 00:00:137.270
proven to work in multiple research studies.

51
00:00:137.270 --> 00:00:139.810
If Prolonged Exposure sounds like it could be right for you,

52
00:00:139.810 --> 00:00:142.480
talk to your doctor about finding a PE provider.

53
00:00:142.480 --> 00:00:145.510
Or, visit the National Center for PTSD website

54
00:00:145.510 --> 00:00:150.980
at www.ptsd.va.gov to learn more about PE and other

55
00:00:150.980 --> 00:00:152.920
PTSD treatment options.

56
00:00:152.920 --> 00:00:155.560
No matter how long you've been living with PTSD,

57
00:00:155.560 --> 00:00:157.190
know that you can get better.
